  "finding": "Redblue can tell you which names are bound (`:vars`) but not what the language itself provides. src/repl/completer.rs completes against keywords, builtins and session bindings, so completion knows the answer and no command exposes it. Comparing against Ipp: `:builtins` and `:modules` are both present there and both absent here (REPL_AUDIT.md sections 2.2 and 2.5). A user cannot answer 'does this language have a regex module?' without leaving the REPL and reading src/stdlib.rs. `:prompt` is missing too, so the prompt string is not configurable - and it is currently a bug, since the banner advertises ':quit' while a bare quit is parsed as a program.",
  "goal": "Add `:builtins` listing every registered builtin with its module, `:modules` listing every module the runtime exposes, and `:prompt` showing or setting the prompt string. All three read from the same registry the completer already uses, so completion and introspection cannot drift apart - if they used separate lists, one would be wrong within a release. `:prompt` defaults to the string that currently works, and setting it must not affect parsing, only display.",
