- Critical candidate: `json.parse` double-wraps errors at `src/runtime.rs:1035` (`.map_err(|e| Error::Runtime(e.to_string(), span))`). `say json.parse("1e400")` renders `Error: RuntimeError: RuntimeError: infinity is not a finite number` with embedded `--> 1:1` then `--> /path:1:1`; same on bytecode VM. Tests in `tests/numeric_edge_test.rs` only check the phrase via `runtime_message`, so the duplication is unasserted.
- Minor candidate: negative-index out-of-bounds message at `src/runtime.rs:129` says `valid indexes are 0 to 2` while negative indexes are documented valid (`SPEC.md:380-381`); `say [1,2,3] at -4` proves it.
- Consistency candidate: formatter deletes all blank lines (`src/formatter.rs`), so `rb format --check` fails on 9 shipped files: `examples/files.rb`, `fizzbuzz.rb`, `formats.rb`, `hello.rb`, `random.rb`, `test_arithmetic.rb`, `time.rb`, `modules/MathUtils.rb`, `modules/SuiteKit.rb`. Diffs are only blank lines (SuiteKit also missing trailing newline).
- Lower-value observations: `and`/`or` do not short-circuit (`say no and (1 / 0) is 0` errors) and are intentionally pinned as non-special by tests but undocumented; `import SuiteKit`/`import MathUtils` from `/tmp` cwd fails `Cannot find module` (root resolution, not established as bug).

